          "context": "## What was asked\n\nName the model that wrote the code from the coding agent itself, so nobody\ntypes it into the command.\n\n## What changed, and why\n\n- Claude Code ends each commit it makes with `Co-Authored-By: <model>\n  <noreply@anthropic.com>`. The gate reads the model from that line, commit\n  by commit, takes the line out of the message, and names the model in\n  `Drafted-by` when it seals the commit. A branch written partly by one\n  model and partly by another says which wrote which.\n- `install-hooks.mjs --claude` adds a Claude Code SessionStart hook to the\n  repository's `.claude/settings.local.json`, kept out of git. As each\n  session starts, the hook hands the session's model to the commands Claude\n  Code runs, as `CHAP_MODEL`: for a single change, and for commits with no\n  line of their own.\n- `--model` counts only where neither says, and the desk shows where the\n  name came from.\n- Model ids read as names in more forms: `claude-sonnet-4-5[1m]`, the\n  Bedrock and Vertex forms, and the older `claude-3-5-sonnet`.\n\n## How it was tested\n\n- The generated code-gate project's tests on Node 22 and Node 20, among\n  them a branch whose two commits Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Sonnet 5.5\n  wrote: each sealed commit names its own model, and a forged `Drafted-by`\n  fails verification. The other templates' tests: all pass.\n- This review, in a copy of the repository with `main` as it stands on\n  GitHub: run without `--model`, the command said \"written by Claude Opus\n  5.5 (from the commits)\", and the sealed commit carried the four lines and\n  no Co-Authored-By line.\n\n## Look closely at\n\n- `code-gate/lib/model.mjs`: which line counts as Claude Code's, and the\n  order of the sources.\n- `describeRange` in `code-gate/lib/range.mjs`, where the line leaves the\n  message."
